// Each wait is in a run of its own. A child that sleeps for a minute: wait_for with 0 says
// it is running without waiting, and with 300 ms after waiting that long. Once it is killed,
// wait_for gives its code without waiting the 60 s it was given. A child that ends after
// half a second wakes a wait_for of a minute then.
//
// The suite has no clock to time a run with, so the program has one: a task that sleeps for
// 200 ms, started just before the wait_for. After a wait_for of 0 it still runs (`waited:
// false`: the wait took less than 200 ms), and after one of 300 ms it has ended (`waited:
// true`: the wait took 200 ms at least, the 100 ms between them being room for the task's
// start). That a wait of a minute ends early is the step's timeout.
// The children are tests/helpers/child.ctx, as `sleep MILLISECONDS CODE`.
//# build child: {home}/tests/helpers/child.ctx
//# build program: main.ctx
//# $ {program} {child} 0
//# timeout: 30
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| true
//| waited: false
//| 137
//# $ {program} {child} 300
//# timeout: 30
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| true
//| waited: true
//| 137
// The child ends with 5 after 500 ms: wait_for gives 5, not null, so it waited until then.
//# $ {program} {child} quick
//# timeout: 30
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| 5
